    "id": "evt_columbia_eaae2d1b",
    "name": "Study Abroad with CET in Italy, Brazil, or Taiwan!",
    "type": "Academic",
    "location_id": "loc_virtual",
    "community_id": "com_columbia_general",
    "description": "&lt;p&gt;Interested in studying abroad in Italy, Brazil, or Taiwan? Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/3ffef103-6688-4a53-8916-9fbff6d908c3@1eb1283f-7a15-43ab-84df-87a2f6ade4fd\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;CET Academic Programs&lt;/a&gt;, which is a study abroad provider that partners with Columbia University to provide enriching, academically rigorous, and immersive Columbia-Approved study abroad opportunities.&amp;nbsp;Attend this session to learn more about all program components, including academics, housing, immersion, extra-curricular and co-curricular opportunities, and the application process.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This information session hosted by Tim Baird, &amp;nbsp;Assistant Director, Institutional Relations at CET,&amp;nbsp;will give a brief overview of the programs (30 minutes) and leave 15 minutes for Q&amp;amp;A.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Please visit the &lt;a href=\"https://global.undergrad.columbia.edu/\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Center for Undergraduate Global Engagement&amp;#39;s&lt;/a&gt; website to learn more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://global.undergrad.columbia.edu/studyabroad/search\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;CET&amp;#39;s Academic Programs&lt;/a&gt;, the application process, and eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp; If you have any questions, please reach out to us at &lt;a href=\"mailto:uge@columbia.edu\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;uge@columbia.edu&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Even if you are unable to attend, we encourage you to register with CET since it will ensure you receive a recording to view at your convenience.&lt;/p&gt;",
